                      <span class="spec_info">the ink field · paper text · del gets its own text-safe values here, since the paper-tuned strike goes invisible on ink · accent text uses text-on-ink-accent, NEVER text-ink-accent: --m-ink-accent is calibrated against the page ground and this band inverts it, so there it resolves to plain ink and vanishes · --m-on-ink-accent is the mirror, the accent in light (~12:1 on the dark band) and the band's own paper ink in dark (where the band is light and yellow would sit near 1.3:1) · the same concession --m-ink-accent makes on paper, one ground further in</span>
